84
00:06:10,519 --> 00:06:11,660
One person only.

85
00:06:13,060 --> 00:06:14,620
Li Xiaorou.

86
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:15,300
Enough, Mom.

87
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:16,319
She didn't even like your post.

88
00:06:16,319 --> 00:06:16,699
All right, all right.

89
00:06:16,699 --> 00:06:17,660
I'm going to sell veggies, Mom. Okay.

90
00:06:24,519 --> 00:06:26,339
Petty trick.

91
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:28,839
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

92
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:29,759
Granny.

93
00:06:29,759 --> 00:06:31,139
Come on, come on, come on.

94
00:06:31,420 --> 00:06:32,079
Walk a little faster.

95
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:33,139
Granny, how much farther?

96
00:06:33,139 --> 00:06:33,560
Walk a little faster.

97
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:34,259
Not far.

98
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:35,600
Almost there.

99
00:06:40,579 --> 00:06:41,060
Wait.

100
00:06:41,699 --> 00:06:42,939
What's the rush, then?

101
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,360
To grab a spot.

102
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:45,939
Get there late and there's no room left.

103
00:06:46,399 --> 00:06:47,540
This is way too rushed.

104
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:49,360
Granny, over here.

105
00:06:49,759 --> 00:06:50,600
Little Zhu. Granny.

106
00:06:51,199 --> 00:06:52,399
Hurry, come over here.

107
00:06:53,519 --> 00:06:54,420
Little Zhu, over here.

108
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:55,800
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

109
00:06:56,839 --> 00:06:58,120
With those legs of yours,

110
00:06:58,620 --> 00:06:59,740
you really can't keep up with your mom.

111
00:06:59,740 --> 00:07:01,120
Your mom always runs out front

112
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:02,240
to grab spots for us.

113
00:07:02,319 --> 00:07:04,240
Kids these days are all so weak.

114
00:07:04,759 --> 00:07:05,339
I'll do it, I'll do it.

115
00:07:05,459 --> 00:07:06,259
What are you standing there for?

116
00:07:06,259 --> 00:07:07,279
Hurry and lay out the veggies.

117
00:07:07,279 --> 00:07:07,660
Learn a thing or two.

118
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:09,379
Come take a look, come take a look.

119
00:07:09,379 --> 00:07:11,060
Home-grown fresh tomatoes.

120
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:12,300
Fresh vegetables.

121
00:07:12,439 --> 00:07:13,399
Mushrooms.

122
00:07:13,959 --> 00:07:15,180
Cheap and good, mushrooms.

123
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:15,939
A little louder.

124
00:07:17,079 --> 00:07:18,060
Louder, come on.

125
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:19,379
Here, let me teach you.

126
00:07:19,459 --> 00:07:19,899
Give it to me.

127
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:23,519
Mushrooms, mushrooms, fresh mushrooms.

128
00:07:23,519 --> 00:07:24,300
That's how you shout it.

129
00:07:24,420 --> 00:07:25,139
A little louder.

130
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:25,740
Come on.

131
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:26,800
Hold it up and shout.

132
00:07:27,079 --> 00:07:29,079
Mushrooms, mushrooms, fresh mushrooms.

133
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,279
That's it. A little louder now.

134
00:07:30,319 --> 00:07:31,199
Our veggies,

135
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:33,319
buy with confidence, eat with ease. Come on.

136
00:07:33,819 --> 00:07:34,899
Get your veggies, get your veggies.

137
00:07:34,939 --> 00:07:36,060
Get your fresh mushrooms.

138
00:07:36,199 --> 00:07:36,879
That's it, that's it.

139
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:37,980
Now you've got it.

140
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:39,240
Organic mushrooms.

141
00:07:39,699 --> 00:07:40,439
Louder.

142
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,240
Freshly picked mushrooms.

143
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:42,160
Selling mushrooms?

144
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:43,079
Yes, ma'am, we sell mushrooms.

145
00:07:43,459 --> 00:07:44,079
Good.

146
00:07:44,279 --> 00:07:44,959
How much per pound?

147
00:07:45,279 --> 00:07:46,720
Just picked, eight yuan a pound.

148
00:07:46,899 --> 00:07:47,500
Two pounds.

149
00:07:47,740 --> 00:07:48,379
That's exactly sixteen.

150
00:07:49,160 --> 00:07:50,399
That's enough, that's enough, just right.

151
00:07:50,519 --> 00:07:51,360
A little more, a little more.

152
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:52,399
Here, here's twenty.

153
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:55,819
Buying veggies?

154
00:07:55,819 --> 00:07:56,519
Ma'am, I...

155
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:58,439
Can I scan four yuan to your phone?

156
00:07:58,759 --> 00:07:59,920
I'm an old lady, I don't have a phone on me.

157
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:01,040
Just give me cash for change.

158
00:08:01,939 --> 00:08:03,160
Here, here, I'll break it for you.

159
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:04,500
Thank you, Granny.

160
00:08:04,779 --> 00:08:05,439
No need to thank me.

161
00:08:06,980 --> 00:08:07,800
Here, count it.

162
00:08:08,879 --> 00:08:10,339
No need to count, it's exactly right.

163
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:11,800
Four yuan change for you, exactly right.

164
00:08:12,279 --> 00:08:12,839
Thank you.

165
00:08:13,220 --> 00:08:13,899
Thank you.

166
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:14,800
Come back again.

167
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:15,459
Sure.

168
00:08:15,459 --> 00:08:16,480
See? We've made our first sale.

169
00:08:16,639 --> 00:08:17,860
I haven't touched cash in ages.

170
00:08:20,639 --> 00:08:21,660
Twenty yuan feels this thick, huh?

171
00:08:27,579 --> 00:08:28,019
Xiaofang

172
00:08:28,259 --> 00:08:28,860
Yang Xiaofang

173
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:31,000
Yang Xiaofang

174
00:08:31,579 --> 00:08:32,139
Uncle

175
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:33,559
You really went to sell vegetables?

176
00:08:33,759 --> 00:08:35,299
The weather changes just like that.

177
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:36,419
Yang Xiaofang

178
00:08:36,419 --> 00:08:37,539
Your luck is about to change too.

179
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:39,279
Your uncle's found you

180
00:08:39,279 --> 00:08:39,940
a new way out.

181
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:41,220
You might be about to strike it rich.

182
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:43,440
Strike it rich? Me?

183
00:08:44,039 --> 00:08:44,779
Today,

184
00:08:44,919 --> 00:08:45,919
I went to the market to sell vegetables.

185
00:08:46,940 --> 00:08:48,600
Someone wanted to buy your herb sachets.

186
00:08:49,039 --> 00:08:50,460
Are these herb sachets yours?

187
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:52,539
These?

188
00:08:52,779 --> 00:08:53,440
They really are mine.

189
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:54,100
Thank you, thank you.

190
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:55,120
Is this one for sale?

191
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:56,879
That one's not for sale.

192
00:08:59,100 --> 00:08:59,700
You want to buy this?

193
00:08:59,779 --> 00:09:00,259
Yes.

194
00:09:00,679 --> 00:09:01,919
However many you have, I'll take them all.

195
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:03,820
She said she'd buy as many as you had.

196
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:06,039
Isn't this the mosquito-repellent sachet

197
00:09:06,039 --> 00:09:07,539
I hung on the baby carrier?

198
00:09:08,980 --> 00:09:09,539
Yes, this one.

199
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:10,279
I didn't even push them.

200
00:09:10,279 --> 00:09:11,539
People came up and asked on their own.

201
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,340
And I got to thinking, usually

202
00:09:13,399 --> 00:09:13,940
you know, the herbs,

203
00:09:13,940 --> 00:09:14,860
after you dry them out,

204
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:16,279
you just sell them to the herb buyers.

205
00:09:16,799 --> 00:09:17,600
But if

206
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:19,000
you make them into sachets,

207
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:21,200
couldn't you earn a bit more?

208
00:09:25,740 --> 00:09:27,659
I think that idea could work.

209
00:09:28,879 --> 00:09:29,720
Right now I need

210
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:30,860
to earn formula money for Bite anyway.

211
00:09:30,899 --> 00:09:32,019
And I can make these right at home.

212
00:09:32,019 --> 00:09:32,639
Exactly.

213
00:09:33,039 --> 00:09:34,299
So I'll make a whole bunch,

214
00:09:34,379 --> 00:09:35,279
and you take them to the market for me

215
00:09:35,279 --> 00:09:35,759
to sell.

216
00:09:35,759 --> 00:09:36,440
Let's see how it goes.

217
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:37,700
If they sell well, you get a cut.

218
00:09:39,279 --> 00:09:39,899
Then tell me,

219
00:09:39,899 --> 00:09:40,700
can you make them fast enough?

220
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:41,639
Don't want demand outpacing supply.

221
00:09:41,700 --> 00:09:42,399
Of course.

222
00:09:43,059 --> 00:09:44,120
How much should I sell them for? Tell me.

223
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:45,820
Five or six bucks.

224
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:48,299
Go a little higher.

225
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:49,139
That's way too low.

226
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,940
You love chicken legs, just like your dad.

227
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:04,580
Just don't end up like him,

228
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:06,139
turning into a lackey.

229
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:11,200
Mom, I want some cola.

230
00:10:21,820 --> 00:10:22,559
Get me a Coke.

231
00:10:24,899 --> 00:10:25,360
Dad.

232
00:10:28,379 --> 00:10:28,860
Mom.

233
00:10:29,340 --> 00:10:30,259
I saw my dad.

234
00:10:30,659 --> 00:10:31,120
Dad!

235
00:10:33,039 --> 00:10:33,500
Dad!

236
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:35,379
Dad!

237
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:37,539
Dad! Qian Zhenqing!

238
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:38,600
Dad!

239
00:10:39,279 --> 00:10:39,820
Dad!

240
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,080
What are you doing?

241
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:44,840
I saw my dad.

242
00:10:46,059 --> 00:10:46,799
Your dad?

243
00:10:49,399 --> 00:10:51,159
He ran off. It was him!

244
00:10:51,799 --> 00:10:52,980
What are you yelling for?

245
00:10:53,519 --> 00:10:54,500
Call anyone but him.

246
00:10:54,799 --> 00:10:55,659
Just pretend he's dead.

247
00:10:56,539 --> 00:10:58,100
I really did see him.

248
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,340
I really saw him.

249
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:00,840
Let's go.

250
00:11:19,559 --> 00:11:20,840
Mom, are you missing Dad?

251
00:11:29,220 --> 00:11:30,259
If I divorced your dad,

252
00:11:30,259 --> 00:11:31,039
who would you go with?

253
00:11:33,980 --> 00:11:34,419
Mom...

254
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:36,820
Are you divorcing Dad?

255
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:42,200
I'm just asking.

256
00:11:43,299 --> 00:11:44,519
Well, definitely not Old Qian.

257
00:11:44,539 --> 00:11:45,100
I'd go with you.

258
00:11:49,820 --> 00:11:52,000
Good boy, you're all I have.

259
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:55,519
Surviving on scraps,

260
00:11:55,519 --> 00:11:57,299
I'll still manage to raise you.

261
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:03,139
With Old Qian, we'd always be hiding,

262
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:04,019
and paying off debts.

263
00:12:04,399 --> 00:12:06,019
Being with you beats being with him.

264
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:10,139
What did you say?

265
00:12:10,679 --> 00:12:11,200
You'd go with me

266
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,559
because you love me more, right?

267
00:12:13,519 --> 00:12:14,340
The two of you...

268
00:12:14,379 --> 00:12:15,120
One's my dad,

269
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:16,220
one's my mom.

270
00:12:16,620 --> 00:12:17,980
I love you both the same.

271
00:12:19,679 --> 00:12:20,220
Mom,

272
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:22,059
divorce him if you want to.

273
00:12:23,019 --> 00:12:24,220
A classmate of mine recently

274
00:12:24,399 --> 00:12:25,279
had his parents split up.

275
00:12:25,860 --> 00:12:27,299
Your own happiness matters most.

276
00:12:28,059 --> 00:12:28,860
Don't overthink it.

277
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:29,879
Really?

278
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,100
Then you'd have no dad anymore.

279
00:12:34,179 --> 00:12:35,120
That's impossible.

280
00:12:35,779 --> 00:12:37,120
Even divorced, he's still my dad.

281
00:12:37,299 --> 00:12:38,460
He's still obligated to support me.

282
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:41,799
So if we two divorce,

283
00:12:41,799 --> 00:12:43,019
what's in it for you?

284
00:12:43,279 --> 00:12:43,799
Go on.

285
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:45,879
Give me a good reason and I'll do it.

286
00:12:48,139 --> 00:12:51,000
At least I'd get double allowance,

287
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:53,399
and double New Year money too.

288
00:12:54,340 --> 00:12:56,360
If you each found someone new,

289
00:12:56,399 --> 00:12:57,720
the inheritance would still be mine, right?

290
00:12:59,059 --> 00:13:00,720
Now you're eyeing the inheritance?

291
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,840
You Heartless little thing!

292
00:13:02,980 --> 00:13:04,340
Just like your damn dad!

293
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:07,340
Are you hoping we divorce soon,

294
00:13:07,340 --> 00:13:08,700
or hoping I die soon?

295
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:10,720
I'll make it hurt!

296
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:11,779
I'll teach you what pain feels like!

297
00:13:11,799 --> 00:13:13,759
You Heartless little brat!

298
00:13:13,779 --> 00:13:14,919
Have mercy on me!

299
00:13:25,279 --> 00:13:26,580
Can we make big money?

300
00:13:27,539 --> 00:13:28,679
Still thinking about money?

301
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:31,700
You Heartless kid.

302
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:33,519
Well, aren't you the same?

303
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:44,919
Hello?

304
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:47,399
Are you selling off your shop?

305
00:13:49,159 --> 00:13:49,620
Yeah, that's right.

306
00:13:57,100 --> 00:13:57,600
Yanyan!

307
00:13:58,320 --> 00:13:59,419
Come here, give me a hug.

308
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:04,299
What are you doing here?

309
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,799
Didn't we agree on this before?

310
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:10,100
We'd come back together after the vacation.

311
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:11,539
You'd introduce me to Mom.

312
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Since when did we go on a vacation?

313
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:14,940
And where is this exactly?

314
00:14:15,620 --> 00:14:16,740
The Maldives bus station?

315
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,700
Well, it's a special situation.

316
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:21,879
I'll make it up to you next time.

317
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:22,600
Here.

318
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:24,000
I bought a whole bunch of stuff.

319
00:14:24,679 --> 00:14:25,440
I remember you saying

320
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:26,340
that Mom loves pastries.

321
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:27,399
So I went out of my way to get some.

322
00:14:27,679 --> 00:14:29,080
Pear syrup candy for the kids.

323
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:31,039
And two bottles of rice wine for your brother.

324
00:14:31,759 --> 00:14:32,980
Over here. Open up the trunk.

325
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:47,980
What's going on here?

326
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:49,440
You lost weight over the holiday?

327
00:14:50,639 --> 00:14:51,779
Have you been working too hard?

328
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:54,200
So you do still care about me.

329
00:14:54,259 --> 00:14:55,080
Whether I'm fat or thin.

330
00:14:56,379 --> 00:14:58,620
Your ex-wife matters more than me.

331
00:14:59,559 --> 00:15:01,279
How could she matter more than you?

332
00:15:02,539 --> 00:15:03,960
Why else would I divorce her?

333
00:15:04,039 --> 00:15:04,500
Right?

334
00:15:05,519 --> 00:15:06,019
Look at you.

335
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:07,740
The second you got mad on the phone,

336
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,379
I dropped everything.

337
00:15:09,460 --> 00:15:10,779
Rushed right over to apologize.

338
00:15:11,519 --> 00:15:11,899
See?

339
00:15:12,379 --> 00:15:13,379
That's how much you mean to me.

340
00:15:17,419 --> 00:15:18,679
A grown woman now,

341
00:15:18,980 --> 00:15:20,139
still acting like a child.

342
00:15:20,379 --> 00:15:21,659
Threatening to break up over nothing.

343
00:15:22,279 --> 00:15:22,759
You've got me...

344
00:15:22,759 --> 00:15:23,919
tossing and turning all night.

345
00:15:24,740 --> 00:15:26,000
I thought you had someone else.

346
00:15:28,279 --> 00:15:28,919
Yanyan.

347
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:30,299
What a coincidence!

348
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:30,879
Old Miao.

349
00:15:31,779 --> 00:15:33,000
Yanyan, who's this?

350
00:15:33,799 --> 00:15:34,320
Yanyan.

351
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:35,179
Who is he?

352
00:15:36,019 --> 00:15:36,559
Um...

353
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:38,320
I shouldn't keep chatting with you.

354
00:15:38,379 --> 00:15:39,240
I'm worried about hitting traffic later.

355
00:15:39,340 --> 00:15:39,919
I'll head off first.

356
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:43,980
Get in the car.

357
00:15:49,100 --> 00:15:50,620
There's no room for me.

358
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:52,820
I mean, couldn't you just...

359
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:53,860
sit in the back?

360
00:15:53,919 --> 00:15:55,120
Why should I sit in the back?

361
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:56,659
Who's this important guest?

362
00:15:56,899 --> 00:15:58,000
Let me give you a ride.

363
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,440
He's a friend of mine.

364
00:16:01,139 --> 00:16:02,100
Dou... Dou Cheng.

365
00:16:03,039 --> 00:16:03,860
Your boyfriend?

366
00:16:05,779 --> 00:16:07,059
The one from Shenzhen?

367
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:08,840
Nice to meet you.

368
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:12,899
Actually, more than a boyfriend.

369
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:15,039
I'm Fan Yan's fiance.

370
00:16:15,559 --> 00:16:17,019
We're getting married soon.

371
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:18,279
After all that,

372
00:16:18,919 --> 00:16:20,120
who exactly are you?

373
00:16:22,460 --> 00:16:23,419
He's my childhood friend.

374
00:16:23,740 --> 00:16:24,580
An old classmate of mine.

375
00:16:26,379 --> 00:16:27,340
More than a classmate.

376
00:16:28,019 --> 00:16:29,659
The kind who grew up together,

377
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:30,940
running around bare-bottomed as kids.

378
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:31,820
What are you saying?

379
00:16:32,419 --> 00:16:33,639
Childhood sweethearts.

380
00:16:34,679 --> 00:16:35,240
Old Miao.

381
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:36,519
Do me a favor.

382
00:16:36,779 --> 00:16:37,799
Somewhere near our place,

383
00:16:37,820 --> 00:16:39,240
find a nice hotel

384
00:16:39,539 --> 00:16:40,460
and get him settled in.

385
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:42,360
The baby at home is so young,

386
00:16:42,539 --> 00:16:43,220
so it's not convenient.

387
00:16:44,159 --> 00:16:45,240
What's so inconvenient about it?

388
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:46,500
Lao Dou.

389
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:47,720
You don't know,

390
00:16:48,179 --> 00:16:49,759
but we have a rule around here.

391
00:16:49,919 --> 00:16:51,080
Until the baby is 100 days old,

392
00:16:51,340 --> 00:16:52,980
no outsiders may enter the house.

393
00:16:53,139 --> 00:16:53,840
I'm an outsider?

394
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:56,919
A friend of Yanyan's

395
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:58,039
is a friend of mine.

396
00:16:58,100 --> 00:16:59,639
I'll get everything sorted for you.

397
00:17:00,179 --> 00:17:01,399
Just stay at our place.

398
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:02,580
The very best room we've got,

399
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:03,600
the Presidential Suite.

400
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:06,759
Old Miao's quite the big spender.

401
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:07,880
What does he do?

402
00:17:08,559 --> 00:17:09,240
A Presidential Suite.

403
00:17:10,039 --> 00:17:10,859
He runs a mine.

404
00:17:12,299 --> 00:17:12,660
Right.

405
00:17:13,299 --> 00:17:14,000
A mine that mines people.

406
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:16,000
He's the head of our village.

407
00:17:16,259 --> 00:17:18,279
Everyone here answers to him.

408
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:20,940
A village head, huh?

409
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:22,240
Then his monthly salary

410
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,559
can't amount to very much.

411
00:17:24,119 --> 00:17:25,220
Then I'd feel even worse

412
00:17:25,220 --> 00:17:26,779
staying in your Presidential Suite.

413
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:32,960
Lao Dou

414
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:35,180
Anyone can tell you're from the big city

415
00:17:35,579 --> 00:17:36,359
Looking down a little

416
00:17:36,359 --> 00:17:37,180
on our little backwater here

417
00:17:38,279 --> 00:17:39,160
But you got it right

418
00:17:39,519 --> 00:17:40,640
Before too long

419
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:42,839
this place will turn into a mining zone

420
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,059
The kind that's

421
00:17:44,339 --> 00:17:45,500
insanely rich, that kind of mine

422
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:45,940
Lao Miao

423
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:47,119
Give me some specifics

424
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:48,160
This place of ours

425
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:50,400
by that Guinness richest man

426
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:51,400
Isn't it Forbes?

427
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:52,900
Right, the Forbes richest man

428
00:17:52,900 --> 00:17:53,519
has taken a liking to it

429
00:17:53,559 --> 00:17:54,960
He wants to turn our Fairy Peak

430
00:17:55,079 --> 00:17:56,000
into the biggest theme park

431
00:17:56,019 --> 00:17:56,960
in the whole world

432
00:17:57,380 --> 00:17:59,099
When it's all theme parks around here

433
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:00,740
what's under our feet then?

434
00:18:01,740 --> 00:18:02,779
It's a gold mine, that's what!

435
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:03,519
Just think about it

436
00:18:03,559 --> 00:18:04,680
Once everyone gets relocated,

437
00:18:05,140 --> 00:18:06,299
every single household here

438
00:18:06,539 --> 00:18:07,720
becomes filthy rich, right?

439
00:18:08,319 --> 00:18:08,700
Yeah

440
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:09,160
Lao Dou

441
00:18:09,480 --> 00:18:10,759
Working in the city

442
00:18:11,539 --> 00:18:12,660
you couldn't make this much money

443
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:14,599
in several lifetimes

444
00:18:15,339 --> 00:18:16,380
Director Miao

445
00:18:17,259 --> 00:18:18,920
then I won't be shy about it

446
00:18:19,579 --> 00:18:21,099
Thanks for the Presidential Suite

447
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:22,779
Lao Dou

448
00:18:23,519 --> 00:18:24,319
Here in our village

449
00:18:25,220 --> 00:18:27,140
whatever you need, just come to me

450
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:29,559
So your name carries weight.

451
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:40,240
Shangri-La

452
00:19:05,859 --> 00:19:06,180
My...

453
00:19:47,140 --> 00:19:48,119
Give me a break.

454
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:50,119
Call this a Presidential Suite?

455
00:19:51,980 --> 00:19:52,960
Waiter!

456
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:07,079
What a dump this place is.

457
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:09,039
Calling itself the Shangri-La Hotel?

458
00:20:09,140 --> 00:20:09,980
And a Presidential Suite, no less.

459
00:20:11,279 --> 00:20:12,519
That Old Miao is a real jerk.

460
00:20:12,640 --> 00:20:13,380
He totally scammed me here.

461
00:20:13,819 --> 00:20:15,220
I'm giving you guys a bad review.

462
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:17,420
Buddy.

463
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:18,960
This crappy hotel, huh?

464
00:20:19,359 --> 00:20:20,140
Let's team up

465
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:21,400
and slam it online.

466
00:20:21,420 --> 00:20:22,059
This lousy hotel.

467
00:20:22,700 --> 00:20:23,819
Forget it, I can't waste time.

468
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:24,700
I'm in the investment business.

469
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:25,619
Time is money.

470
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:27,240
Investing?

471
00:20:27,359 --> 00:20:27,839
What about it?

472
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:30,440
What's worth investing in around this dump?

473
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:33,980
Did you hear

474
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:34,880
about the amusement park deal too?

475
00:20:35,819 --> 00:20:36,579
You know what,

476
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:37,880
once this big park gets built,

477
00:20:38,099 --> 00:20:38,880
the crowds will come.

478
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:40,619
And once the crowds come, so does the money.

479
00:20:42,099 --> 00:20:42,740
An amusement park.

480
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:45,299
This lousy little place?

481
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:47,380
They're building the world's biggest park here.

482
00:20:48,140 --> 00:20:49,839
Every village on the mountain gets demolished.

483
00:20:50,279 --> 00:20:51,359
Every household gets compensation.

484
00:20:52,220 --> 00:20:53,079
Who'd have thought

485
00:20:53,519 --> 00:20:54,680
sticking with some run-down village

486
00:20:54,839 --> 00:20:55,900
would actually pay off?

487
00:20:57,700 --> 00:20:58,440
No wonder.

488
00:20:59,859 --> 00:21:01,380
No wonder she wants to divorce me.

489
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:02,180
The papers I asked for,

490
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:03,539
you never gave me all along.

491
00:21:06,559 --> 00:21:07,039
Yanyan

492
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:08,619
This dump is impossible to live in

493
00:21:09,059 --> 00:21:09,880
I'm heading to your place today

494
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:11,160
Come pick me up

495
00:21:11,579 --> 00:21:12,980
I'm busy, it's not convenient

496
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:14,039
I can't come get you

497
00:21:15,220 --> 00:21:16,740
If you're busy, go do your thing

498
00:21:17,420 --> 00:21:18,619
I'll just chat with your mom

499
00:21:20,059 --> 00:21:21,579
We have our own local customs here

500
00:21:22,339 --> 00:21:23,640
When there's a newborn in the house,

501
00:21:23,839 --> 00:21:25,000
we don't receive outsiders

502
00:21:25,579 --> 00:21:27,160
I only took a few days off

503
00:21:28,019 --> 00:21:28,859
The hospital's waiting for me too

504
00:21:28,859 --> 00:21:29,640
I've got to get back and take care of things

505
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:31,220
It's not like I invited you here

506
00:21:31,579 --> 00:21:32,799
If you're busy, go handle your stuff

507
00:21:33,460 --> 00:21:34,500
Just head on home

508
00:21:35,079 --> 00:21:36,099
That's all, hanging up now

509
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:37,319
Yanyan

510
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:41,279
I came all this way,

511
00:21:41,319 --> 00:21:43,000
and you just toss me aside

512
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:44,299
Who does that?

513
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:45,819
Mom

514
00:21:46,740 --> 00:21:47,440
So this is Lao Dou?

515
00:21:48,559 --> 00:21:49,779
He's not even fifty

516
00:21:49,799 --> 00:21:50,339
About right

517
00:21:50,579 --> 00:21:51,839
Why does he look so old?

518
00:21:52,859 --> 00:21:54,059
Well, he's got plenty of hair

519
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:55,660
Auntie

520
00:21:55,779 --> 00:21:57,359
Since Lao Dou's come to visit,

521
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:58,559
he owes me a red envelope, right?

522
00:21:59,279 --> 00:22:01,000
The kid really takes after her mother

523
00:22:01,039 --> 00:22:02,079
All you think about is money

524
00:22:02,579 --> 00:22:03,380
And calling him Lao Dou?

525
00:22:03,619 --> 00:22:04,579
Show some manners

526
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:06,240
That's your uncle

527
00:22:06,380 --> 00:22:07,579
Uncle, my foot

528
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:09,240
Nothing's settled yet

529
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:10,519
Don't call him uncle

530
00:22:13,180 --> 00:22:13,920
What's wrong?

531
00:22:14,839 --> 00:22:16,299
He's already come to visit,

532
00:22:16,700 --> 00:22:17,680
and now you're playing hard to get?

533
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:21,099
Just because he showed up, I have to fawn over him?

534
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:22,380
Is he Andy Lau?

535
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:23,380
Or Jiang Wen?

536
00:22:24,019 --> 00:22:24,900
Why should I?

537
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:26,460
You don't get it, this guy

538
00:22:27,019 --> 00:22:27,759
isn't even that old,

539
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,599
but he carries himself like an old man

540
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:30,400
Look,

541
00:22:30,619 --> 00:22:31,819
we're not getting any younger,

542
00:22:33,700 --> 00:22:35,500
we've been dating for two years,

543
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:37,579
and now you say he seems old?

544
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:39,039
Where was this thought before?

545
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:40,640
Were you dating with your eyes closed?

546
00:22:40,799 --> 00:22:41,500
Well, yeah

547
00:22:41,779 --> 00:22:42,779
Cupid, the god of love,

548
00:22:42,799 --> 00:22:43,900
he's blind, isn't he?

549
00:22:45,220 --> 00:22:46,339
Now you and Yang Xiaofang

550
00:22:46,339 --> 00:22:47,259
have switched places

551
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:49,079
She's come around,

552
00:22:49,420 --> 00:22:50,460
and now you're the one who can't

553
00:22:51,359 --> 00:22:52,299
But honestly,

554
00:22:52,920 --> 00:22:53,759
do you think

555
00:22:53,819 --> 00:22:55,599
Yang Xiaofang and Xiaowei still have a shot?

556
00:22:56,299 --> 00:22:57,339
If you ask me,

557
00:22:57,660 --> 00:22:58,940
I'm quite fond of Xiaowei

558
00:23:00,720 --> 00:23:01,940
What good is you being fond of him?

559
00:23:02,099 --> 00:23:02,799
What matters is

560
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:04,259
whether Yang Xiaofang likes him

561
00:23:05,980 --> 00:23:08,500
You should worry about your own affairs

562
00:23:09,059 --> 00:23:10,259
So how's things with Old Qian?

563
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:12,740
Are you still seeing Dou Cheng or not?

564
00:23:15,220 --> 00:23:17,079
Mind your own business

565
00:23:19,420 --> 00:23:21,099
Fine, one problem down

566
00:23:26,160 --> 00:23:26,980
She's unreachable.

567
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:28,519
She just disappeared.

568
00:23:29,180 --> 00:23:31,119
I came all this way to see her,

569
00:23:31,759 --> 00:23:32,420
and what does she do?

570
00:23:32,940 --> 00:23:34,359
She just left me hanging here.

571
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:35,680
What's the point of all this?

572
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:37,420
I'm leaving at dawn.

573
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:39,920
Then you came all this way for nothing.

574
00:23:41,099 --> 00:23:41,960
This thing between you two,

575
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:42,980
I get it now.

576
00:23:43,619 --> 00:23:44,240
The problem is you.

577
00:23:45,180 --> 00:23:45,980
Women, you know,

578
00:23:46,319 --> 00:23:47,440
they love a little romance,

579
